.idea
node_modules/
state.json
state.json.tmp
# runtime persistence beside state.json — queued-turn journal + per-project report drafts:
queue.jsonl
drafts/
# per-month usage metering (token/cost attribution — see docs/multitenancy.md §7):
usage/
# per-month answer feedback (the value side of the same metering — see feedback.ts):
feedback/
.release
projects.config.json
# local-dev per-project prompt files (an installation's live in its overlay, infra/<slug>/projects.d/):
/projects.d/
# per-project memory journals (server-owned git repos; like state.json, never committed):
memory/
# per-project derived facts (facts/<slug>.json — machine-written, re-derivable; see docs/project-facts.md):
facts/
*.log
# secrets — standalone repo, so ignore them here (no parent repo to do it):
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
github-app-private-key.pem
# infra/ is an ALLOW-LIST: every installation's ops repo is checked out at infra/<slug>/
# (infra/deploy/README.md; template in infra/deploy/ops.example/) and must never be staged —
# whatever the slug, so this file names no installation. Only the public tooling is tracked:
infra/*
!infra/README.md
!infra/deploy/
!infra/teams/
# Terraform working files anywhere (a module's init cache, a root's state — state holds secrets):
.terraform/
.terraform.lock.hcl
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
/.claude/worktrees/transparency-trail/
/.claude/worktrees/youtrack-rich-context/
events/
data/

# the mirror job's cache (bare repos + log) of an installation whose directory is this checkout
/mirrors/
/mirrors.json
# the compose runtime's files of such an installation (OpenSpec container-deploy): the rendered
# compose.yaml + the version pin, and the deploy log
/compose/
/deploys.log
